    "updated_at": "2022-01-21T02:36:31Z",
    "body": "> I keep all my dotfiles in a git repository, so I don't really want the configuration file to change all the time, so the information for the current state of the prompt could be saved in `$XDG_STATE_HOME`.\n> \n\nIf you want a temporary config, you can copy your existing config file over and set `$STARSHIP_CONFIG` to that copy. Then you can use `starship toggle` without changing your actual dotfiles. ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
