    "updated_at": "2022-01-22T07:45:47Z",
    "body": "I get it, you want multiple format strings you can switch between.\n\nI'm just saying this can already be archived today, with a hand-rolled shell function that runs `starship toggle`, `starship config`, `sed` or whatever method to modify your current config to your liking.\n\nOr if you don't want to mess up with current config, use a temporary file and set `$STARSHIP_CONFIG` to that. \n\nNote that even with #3467 you still need to tell the prompt function of your current shell what profile to use, either by overriding it or via an environment variable. This is not _much_ different from the solution described above. \n\n_Not that I'm against adding features to Starship, just want to remind you of the UNIX way to compose stuff together. The most featureful solution is what you make yourself with the building blocks._",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
