    "created_at": "2022-04-24T00:19:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-24T00:19:50Z",
    "body": "For those using nix(-shell and friends), here is something to allow overriding per `nix-shell`... which also considers the specified user's configuration.\r\n\r\nSomething something \"a nix-shell should not access a user's configuration\", blah blah blah.\r\n\r\nThis seems to work for me, anyhow:\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><code>shell.nix</code></summary>\r\n\r\n```nix\r\n{ oxalica ? import (builtins.fetchTarball \"https://github.com/oxalica/rust-overlay/archive/master.tar.gz\")\r\n, pkgs ? import <nixpkgs> {\r\n    overlays = [\r\n      oxalica\r\n    ];\r\n  }\r\n, config ? import <nixpkgs/nixos> { }\r\n, ...\r\n}:\r\nlet\r\n  latestStable = pkgs.rust-bin.stable.latest.default.override {\r\n    extensions = [ \"rust-src\" \"rust-std\" \"rustfmt-preview\" \"clippy-preview\" ];\r\n  };\r\n  tomlFormat = pkgs.formats.toml { };\r\n  starshipConfigOverride = {\r\n    line_break = {\r\n      disbled = false;\r\n    };\r\n    localip = {\r\n      disabled = true;\r\n    };\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  starshipConfigDefault =\r\n    config.config.home-manager.users.evanjs.programs.starship.settings;\r\n\r\n  mergedStarshipConfig = starshipConfigDefault // starshipConfigOverride;\r\n\r\n  processStarshipConfig = name: settings:\r\n    tomlFormat.generate name settings;\r\n\r\n  processedStarshipConfig = processStarshipConfig \"starship-config-final\" mergedStarshipConfig;\r\n\r\nin\r\nwith pkgs;\r\n\r\nstdenv.mkDerivation {\r\n  name = \"rust-env\";\r\n  buildInputs = [\r\n    latestStable\r\n    openssl\r\n    bashInteractive\r\n  ];\r\n\r\n  nativeBuildInputs = [\r\n    pkgconfig\r\n  ];\r\n\r\n  CARGO_NET_GIT_FETCH_WITH_CLI = \"true\";\r\n\r\n  STARSHIP_CONFIG = processedStarshipConfig;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nIn the above example, the specified starship settings for the specified user (`evanjs`) will be copied and then [updated](https://nixos.wiki/wiki/Nix_Expression_Language#Operators) with the settings specified in the config override.\r\n\r\nThe final expression will then be converted to TOML, written to the Nix store, and available via the `STARSHIP_CONFIG` variable, which is then used by starship while in the nix shell.\r\n\r\nThis can be used to both toggle modules or just customize various other settings.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
